Well, I thought cursed ones at first, but then I thought that people
may complain about the possibility of, say, an arch-lich (especially if
they don't like genociding them as it makes it 'too easy', hah)
summoning stuff, then cursing the stuff, cursing the boots, and
rendering them really slow while they get attacked by a ton of stuff
before they can uncurse them.

After typing that out, I just realised that if they kept them blessed,
then there wouldn't be especially as much of a threat...

The only other time cursedness/negative-enchantedness would come into
play is randomly generated ones; it's unlikely for someone to make
their own boots negatively enchanted, and as negatively enchanted stuff
is always generated cursed (IIRC), it'd only really happen with putting
on random speed boots (which'd serve them right).

I don't know, it's a toss up between cursed and negatively enchanted.

Actually, another argument against enchantment is that it'd imply that
+0 speed boots should have no effect.



